<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="051" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rewrite mcp-tool-handler; update widget and DA skills</title>
    <phase>E Docs and terminology</phase>
    <gate>after 042, 043 and 050</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Skill documentation rewrites with explicit constraints (naming note, real file paths)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Documentation rewrite from implemented code and the naming note</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>M</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches .claude/ — main-session-only (permission boundary, root CLAUDE.md §3)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>042, 043, 050</deps>
    <tags>documentation, config</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Rewrite .claude/skills/mcp-tool-handler to the real conventions this project built, and update widget-design (URI, folder, size budget) and declarative-agent (current schemas, MCP action) so future sessions follow what the code does.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in maintaining Spaarke's AI procedure skills.</role>
  <goal>The three skills describe the implemented conventions with paths that exist; .claude/CHANGELOG.md records the change; doc-drift-audit reports no stale reference in them.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-18; naming note §1 (tool names in mcp-tool-handler; widget URI, folder and size in widget-design). Code is the source of truth (root CLAUDE.md §2).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">.claude/skills/mcp-tool-handler/SKILL.md (rewrite)</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/skills/widget-design/SKILL.md</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/skills/declarative-agent/SKILL.md</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/CHANGELOG.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/ (implemented host, tools and resource)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/ (implemented widget)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/ and src/solutions/CopilotAgent/ (packages)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="042" status="pending">Live-verified conventions</dependency>
      <dependency task="043" status="pending">Agent schemas if built (cancelled is fine)</dependency>
      <dependency task="050" status="pending">.claude/CHANGELOG.md edited first</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">mcp-tool-handler states: tool names spaarke_{verb}_{object}; routes /mcp/{area} with tools grouped under Api/Mcp/{Area}/{Group}/ and discovered per area; explicit readOnlyHint, title and a 'use for / not for' description of at most 1,024 characters; app-only visibility for widget-only tools; errors as isError via DecisionResultMapper → McpToolResults; FR-04-style minimum text for model-visible output; the tests a new tool needs (auth, contract, size, arch guard, conformance).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">widget-design states: ui://spaarke/{widget}.html; source folder src/client/widgets/{skill-name}/; aim under 1 MB, fail above 3 MB (with Phase 0's measured init times); host theme only; empty csp; callServerTool-only shims returning Response.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">declarative-agent states the schema versions actually used (DA v1.9, plugin v2.4, manifest 1.30 if 043 was built) and keeps 'Spaarke AI' as the agent name.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every path named in the three skills exists (doc-drift-audit clean); main session only (root CLAUDE.md §3).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/mcp-tool-handler/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/widget-design/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/declarative-agent/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ai-procedure-maintenance/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/doc-drift-audit/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/coordination/2026-11-06-copilot-naming-and-ownership.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/phase0-results.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the three skills and the implemented code they describe.</step>
    <step order="2">Rewrite mcp-tool-handler; update widget-design and declarative-agent; update each skill's last-reviewed date.</step>
    <step order="3">Apply the ai-procedure-maintenance checklist for skill edits; add the .claude/CHANGELOG.md entry.</step>
    <step order="4">Run doc-drift-audit on the three skills and fix every stale reference.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a convention in the naming note and the implemented code disagree, STOP and ask the owner which wins (code wins by default, root CLAUDE.md §2).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands (grep, wc, git diff)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">.claude/skills/mcp-tool-handler/SKILL.md</output>
    <output type="docs">.claude/skills/widget-design/SKILL.md</output>
    <output type="docs">.claude/skills/declarative-agent/SKILL.md</output>
    <output type="docs">.claude/CHANGELOG.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">mcp-tool-handler covers every item in its constraint above and every path it names exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">widget-design covers every item in its constraint above, including the measured size and init numbers.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">declarative-agent states the schema versions actually used and the 'Spaarke AI' name.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">doc-drift-audit reports no stale reference in the three skills.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">.claude/CHANGELOG.md has an entry for the three skill changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: none of the three skills uses 'Spaarke Copilot' as a name or the April camelCase tool naming as the convention.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Main session only. Run after 050 (both edit .claude/CHANGELOG.md).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist. Main session only (touches .claude/; sub-agents are denied — root CLAUDE.md §3).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
